; The negative product at a boundary, on the native Java target.
;
; The JVM has no multiple return, so the compiler builds one out of a record —
; shared by result SHAPE, so two functions returning (int int) use one type.
;
; This file exists to answer ONE question. product-2026-08-19 measured C2
; scalar-replacing a record returned from a hot call at 0.96x, INSIDE THE NOISE
; — but that was a record and a caller in the same source file. Whether the
; escape analysis still fires when the record is generated by us and the caller
; is hand-written in another class is what nobody has measured, and it is the
; reason the first attempt at this feature dodged Java entirely.

(use java)

(export divmod divmod-sum)

(sig divmod     ((a int) (b int)) (int int) (where (java.!= b 0)))
; THE SUM NEEDS A BOUND ON `a`, and 2^52-1 is derived rather than picked.
; `q` is a/b and `r` is a%b, so |q| <= |a| and |r| <= |a| whatever b is --
; therefore |q + r| <= 2|a|, and the sum stays inside ADR 0012's window exactly
; when |a| <= (2^53-1)/2. Bounding `b` as well buys nothing: the analysis gets
; both the quotient and the remainder from `a` alone.
;
; Without it this is REFUSED, which is ADR 0019 working -- outside the window Go
; and the JVM wrap and JavaScript loses precision, so the program has to say
; what it means.
(sig divmod-sum ((a (int -4503599627370495 4503599627370495)) (b int)) int
  (where (java.!= b 0)))

(def dm (fn (a b) (values (java./ a b) (java.% a b))))

(def divmod     (fn (a b) (dm a b)))
(def divmod-sum (fn (a b) ((dm a b) (fn (q r) (java.+ q r)))))
